# Setlist Archive URLs (/archive)

All URL slugs for **Setlist Archive** pages must start with `/archive`.

## Convention

- **Base path**: `/archive`
- **`public/_redirects`**: Profile tab paths (`/archive/profile/overview`, etc.) and public user paths (`/archive/user/...`) normalize to query forms. There are **no** `/old/archive` → `/archive` migration redirects (pre-launch site).
- **Examples**:
  - Years: `/archive/years?id={uuid}` — use `getYearArchiveUrl(yearId)` from `lib/year-archive-url.ts`. Old path form `/archive/years/{uuid}` has no blanket redirect; migrate the route or add a rule when ready.
  - Tours: `/archive/tours?id={uuid}` — use `getTourArchiveUrl(tourId)` from `lib/tour-archive-url.ts`. Same for legacy `/archive/tours/{uuid}`.
  - Songs index: `/archive/songs`. **Song detail**: `/archive/song?id={uuid}` — use `getSongArchiveUrl(songId)` from `lib/song-archive-url.ts`. Same for legacy `/archive/song/{uuid}`.
  - Stats: `/archive/stats`, **Personnel index**: `/archive/personnel`. **Personnel detail**: `/archive/personnel?id={uuid}` — use `getPersonnelArchiveUrl(guestId)` from `lib/personnel-archive-url.ts`. Same for legacy `/archive/personnel/{uuid}`.
  - **Venues index**: `/archive/venues`. **Venue detail**: `/archive/venue?id={venue_id or venue name}` — use `getVenueArchiveUrl(venueKey)` from `lib/venue-archive-url.ts`. Same for legacy `/archive/venue/{segment}`.
  - **Discography index**: `/archive/discography`. **Discography release**: `/archive/discography?id={uuid}` — use `getDiscographyArchiveUrl(releaseUuid)` from `lib/discography-archive-url.ts`. Same for legacy `/archive/discography/{uuid}`.
  - **Lists index**: `/archive/lists`. **List detail**: `/archive/lists?id={uuid}` — use `getListArchiveUrl(listId)` from `lib/list-archive-url.ts`. Same for legacy `/archive/lists/{uuid}`.
  - **Setlist Game index**: `/archive/setlistgame`. **Per-show game**: `/archive/setlistgame?id={show_id}` — `getSetlistGameShowArchiveUrl` from `lib/setlist-game-archive-url.ts`. **Per-tour game**: `/archive/setlistgame?tour_id={tour_id}` — `getSetlistGameTourArchiveUrl`. Same for legacy path-style setlist game URLs.
  - **My Stats (signed-in)**: `/archive/profile?tab={slug}` — same tab slugs as public profiles. Path-style `/archive/profile/{tab}` **301** in `public/_redirects` to `?tab=`.
  - **Public user stats**: `/user?id={user_uuid}&tab={slug}` (`overview`, `shows`, `songs`, `slots`, `personnel`, `badges`; legacy `loose-ends` **301** / canonicalized to `badges`) — use `getUserProfileUrl` from `lib/user-profile-url.ts`. `/archive/user` **301** to `/user` with merged query in `public/_redirects`. Legacy `/user/{uuid}` **301** to `?id=`.
  - Submit: `/archive/submit`
  - **Show setlist (per-show)**: `/archive/setlist?id={uuid}` — use `getSetlistArchiveUrl(showId)` from `lib/setlist-archive-url.ts` for every internal link. Static export cannot add new `generateStaticParams` entries after deploy; query-based URLs avoid that. **Legacy** `?show_id=` is still accepted on the client and replaced with `?id=` for the same value.

## Implementation

- **App Router**: Setlist Archive under `app/(wl-home-v2)/archive/...`. My Stats: `app/(wl-home-v2)/archive/profile/page.tsx` (query `tab`). Public profile: `app/(wl-home-v2)/user/page.tsx`.
- **Links**: Use `/archive/...` and the `get*ArchiveUrl` helpers above for internal links (show setlist, year, tour on archive, song, personnel, list, venue, discography, setlist game show/tour). For public user profile links, use `getUserProfileUrl`.
- **Breadcrumbs**: For any Setlist Archive page, the first breadcrumb segment after Home must show **"Setlist Archive"** (not "Dpro"); link target remains `/archive`.
- **Pathname checks**: Treat `pathname.startsWith("/archive")` as “user is in B” for sidebar expansion and active state.

## Checklist when adding or changing Setlist Archive routes

- [ ] Route path starts with `/archive`
- [ ] Sidebar nav uses `/archive/...` for the corresponding item
- [ ] Any internal links to setlist pages use `/archive/...`
